 {
  "coord": "2:19",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "reversal",
  "note": "\"Force me to keep you\" means you force me; candidate has Hermione forcing him.",
  "replacement": "HERMIONE. \"Truly\"! You put me off with limp vows. But even if you tried to knock the stars out of their spheres with oaths, I would still say, \"Sir, no going.\" Truly, you shall not go. A lady's \"truly\" is as powerful as a lord's. Will you go still? Then you force me to keep you as a prisoner, not a guest, and you'll pay your fees when you leave and save your thanks. What do you say? My prisoner or my guest? By your dreaded \"truly,\" you shall be one of them."
 },
