 {
  "coord": "2:33",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "invention",
  "note": "\"A thousand furlongs\" became \"a thousand miles\", changing the figure.",
  "replacement": "HERMIONE. What! Have I twice said well? When was the first time? Please tell me. Cram us with praise and make us as fat as tame things. One good deed dying unspoken slaughters a thousand waiting on it. Our praises are our wages. You can ride us a thousand furlongs with one soft kiss, before we'd cover an acre when heated by the spur. But to the goal. My last good deed was to ask him to stay. What was my first? It has an elder sister, or I misunderstand you. Oh, I wish her name were Grace! But once before I spoke to the purpose. When? No, let me have it; I long to know."
 },
